                <pb facs="0858" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg776"/>

                <head>[Extract. —Translation]</head>
                <p>In a despatch from St. Nazaire we noticed that the Louisiana, of the General
                    Transatlantic Company, went to sea yesterday at three o’clock. She took the
                    first detachment of six hundred men of the Belgian legion enrolled for Mexico,
                    one hundred and seventy-eight civilian passengers, and a full cargo of
                    merchandise and material exported for carrying on of the war.</p>

                <p>General Count de Thun has arrived in Paris, charged by the Mexican government to
                    come to an arrangement with the Transatlantic Steam Navigation Company for the
                    conveyance to Yera Cruz of four thousand two hundred volunteers, enlisted in
                    Austria.</p>
            </div>
